---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="What I help with · Direct Lifestyle Medicine" active="help" bookbar={true}>

  <!-- 1 · Intro -->
  <section class="page-title">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>What I help with</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Three parts of one practice. Every member gets the first. The
        other two come in when your health needs them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · Prevention and lifestyle medicine -->
  <section class="section band-tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">One</span>
        <h2>Prevention and lifestyle medicine</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Where everyone starts. We look at how you live, find what is
          hurting your health, and change it in an order you can
          manage.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps c3">
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Nutrition and metabolic health</h4>
          <p>Food, blood sugar, cholesterol, weight. Practical changes to
          how you eat.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Movement</h4>
          <p>Activity that fits your body, your schedule, and what you
          will keep doing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Sleep</h4>
          <p>How much, how good, and what is interrupting it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Stress and emotional health</h4>
          <p>What is weighing on you and how it shows up in your body.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>People around you</h4>
          <p>Relationships and support. They affect your health too.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Alcohol, tobacco, and other habits</h4>
          <p>Practical steps, without lectures.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rows" style="margin-top:clamp(30px,4vw,46px)">
        <div class="row">
          <b>A full assessment first</b>
          <p>Your history, medicines, conditions, risks, and the doctors
          you already see. Then screenings and tests that are due.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>A written plan</b>
          <p>What we are working on, in what order, who does what, and
          when we check. It changes as you do.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Goals we measure</b>
          <p>Blood pressure, labs, weight, sleep, how you feel. We look
          at them together and adjust.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · Medical care and treatment -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Two</span>
        <h2>Medical care and treatment</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Lifestyle medicine is how I approach your care. It is not a
          rule against medicine. When testing or treatment is needed, I
          use it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rows">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Evaluation and diagnosis</b>
          <p>You bring a symptom or a concern. I examine, test, and
          find the cause.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Conditions I manage</b>
          <p>High blood pressure, diabetes and prediabetes, cholesterol,
          thyroid, obesity, acid reflux, and other conditions within my
          scope. Some conditions need a specialist leading, and I will
          tell you when yours does.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Medicines</b>
          <p>Started, adjusted, stopped, and monitored. I review all of
          them together for what is working, what is not needed, and what
          interacts. This includes weight-loss medicines when they
          fit.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Labs and imaging</b>
          <p>I order what is needed, tell you the price first where I
          can, and explain every result.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Abnormal findings</b>
          <p>I explain every abnormal result, and we decide together
          what to do next.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Everyday illness</b>
          <p>Infections, rashes, stomach trouble, and injuries that do
          not need an ER, when I am available.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · Care coordination -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Three</span>
        <h2>Care coordination</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Included in the membership. If you see more than one
          clinician, I help keep your care connected.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rows">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Working with your primary care doctor</b>
          <p>If you have one, I send them a summary after your first
          visit, with your permission, and keep them informed. I do not
          repeat their work or ask you to choose.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Working with specialists</b>
          <p>I talk to them, read what they send, and add it to your
          plan.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Referrals</b>
          <p>When you need another kind of doctor, I refer you and stay
          involved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>If I am your only doctor</b>
          <p>I provide the care I can and help you set up whatever else
          you need. You can join without another doctor.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Following up</b>
          <p>I order tests, track results, and check that treatment is
          working. When you need other clinicians or a higher level of
          care, I hand you off.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · Common situations -->
  <section class="section" id="bookbar-after">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>Common situations</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards c3">
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;It&rsquo;s several things at once.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Blood pressure, weight, sleep, stress. We sort out what is
            urgent, what matters most, and what can wait. Then we work
            through it in order.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;I don&rsquo;t have a doctor right now.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            You can join without one. I provide the preventive and
            medical care I can, and help you set up anything else you
            need.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;I have a doctor and want more help between visits.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Keep them. I add evaluation, treatment within my scope, and
            coordination with them.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;Something came back abnormal.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            A lab or scan you want to understand. I go through what it
            means, what to do next, and what to watch.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;I want my conditions closely managed.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Diabetes, blood pressure, cholesterol, thyroid. I review
            medicines, watch for complications, and track your numbers
            against the goals we set.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;My health and my life are tangled together.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Stress affects sleep. Sleep affects eating. Money worries
            affect all of it. We treat what needs treating and work on
            the rest one step at a time. When you need a counselor or a
            financial professional, I help you find one and stay
            involved.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · What I don't do -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>What I don&rsquo;t do</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            This membership is not a promise to manage every medical
            condition you have.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
        <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Emergencies</b>
          <p>Chest pain, stroke signs, severe injury: call 911 or go to
          the ER. Afterward, I help you understand what happened.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Hospital care</b>
          <p>The hospital&rsquo;s doctors run the admission. I stay
          informed and manage your care when you&rsquo;re home.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Specialist-led conditions, alone</b>
          <p>Some conditions need an oncologist or cardiologist leading.
          I refer you, share your care with them, and stay involved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Mental health care beyond my scope</b>
          <p>For serious psychiatric illness, or addiction care beyond
          what I can safely provide, I help you find the right care and
          hand you off directly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Children</b>
          <p>Adults only (18+).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7 · CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>Not sure if your situation fits?</h2>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
        <p style="margin-top:22px"><a class="quiet" href="/how-it-works">How the membership works &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
